+# TLS Backend Policy
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use rustls as its TLS backend. It was chosen because it is a pure Rust implementation with no native C library dependency, which reduces the project's security surface area and removes the class of memory-safety vulnerabilities associated with native TLS libraries.
